From: Jonas Heinle <jonasheinle@googlemail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 20:21:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Define AbstractOperatorDesc's members where OperatorField is
 complete

AbstractOperatorDesc holds a std::vector<OperatorField> while OperatorField is
only forward-declared, and defines its special members inline. precomp.h
includes AbstractOperatorDesc.h before GeneratedSchemaTypes.h, so the first
use through std::optional<AbstractOperatorDesc> instantiates the vector's
destructor and move operations against the incomplete type. MSVC does not
diagnose this because it defers those instantiations to the end of the
translation unit; clang-cl reports the incomplete type.

Declare the special members, the four tensor accessors and GetTensors() in the
class, and define them at the end of GeneratedSchemaTypes.h, immediately after
OperatorField becomes complete. No behaviour change.

Assisted-by: Claude (Anthropic)
---
 .../DirectMLHelpers/AbstractOperatorDesc.h    | 69 ++++---------------
 .../DirectMLHelpers/GeneratedSchemaTypes.h    | 63 +++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 77 insertions(+), 55 deletions(-)

